### name: sort-take.scalar-source-through-a-variable
--- note
A first argument with no children is a one-element list when it has a scalar and an empty list when it is NONE (7.3), for every aggregate. The sorts, TOP* and BUCKET treated a scalar as empty in most hosts (lisp/go for TOP, five hosts for BUCKET); C++ alone followed the text. The fused and the unfused spelling must agree.
