--- expect
tree -{"1"=t"str"}
===
### name: sort.scalar-then-filter-non-bool-is-an-error
--- note
A first argument with no children is a one-element list when it has a scalar and an empty list when it is NONE (7.3), for every aggregate. The sorts, TOP* and BUCKET treated a scalar as empty in most hosts (lisp/go for TOP, five hosts for BUCKET); C++ alone followed the text. The one element reaches FILTER, whose predicate is not BOOL: optimised or not, E_NOT_BOOL at the predicate.
--- source
S = "str"; S .> SORT .> FILTER(1) .> TAKE(5)
--- expect
error E_NOT_BOOL at 1:32
===
