--- source
COUNT(SORT(NULL))
--- expect
num 0
===
### name: sort.empty-text-is-a-one-element-list
--- note
A first argument with no children is a one-element list when it has a scalar and an empty list when it is NONE (7.3), for every aggregate. The sorts, TOP* and BUCKET treated a scalar as empty in most hosts (lisp/go for TOP, five hosts for BUCKET); C++ alone followed the text. The empty string is a scalar.
--- source
COUNT(SORT(""))
--- expect
num 1
===
### name: sort.empty-list
--- note
An empty list sorts to an empty list.
--- source
COUNT(SORT(LIST()))
--- expect
num 0
===
